.TH grokbot-tui-mcp 1  "mcp " 
.SH NAME
grokbot\-tui\-mcp \- MCP server for other agents (Claude Code, Cursor, ...): `mcp serve [\-\-stdio|\-\-http [ADDR]]`, `mcp token`, `mcp config`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgrokbot\-tui mcp\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
MCP server for other agents (Claude Code, Cursor, ...): `mcp serve [\-\-stdio|\-\-http [ADDR]]`, `mcp token`, `mcp config`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
grokbot\-tui\-mcp\-serve(1)
Run the MCP server (stdio by default; \-\-http for streamable HTTP on localhost)
.TP
grokbot\-tui\-mcp\-token(1)
Print the HTTP bearer token (created on first use) for a client\*(Aqs config
.TP
grokbot\-tui\-mcp\-config(1)
Show the MCP settings in use and where they live
